    comment "en" """
        Source = skills training in going up and down stairs. SNOMED CT 229608007 (@sv: gångträning i
        trappa), active procedure. Exact : direct concept + Swedish-synonym match for stair-climbing
        training; one-level-broader model framing (procedure vs skills training) holds it below.
        """
}
mapping "VA2.AT.ZZ.1" source="VA2.AT.ZZ" target="SNOMED_CT:370854007" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source VA2.AT.ZZ SNOMED CT 370854007 = a Swedish social-service information-gathering activity from
        a professional informant regarding the combined lifestyle-behavior cluster (alcohol, narcotics,
        tobacco, doping/doping agents, gambling). Target is the closest standard procedure for a
        multi-substance behavioral information-gathering activity, but it covers only the substance axis
        (alcohol/narcotics/tobacco), omitting doping-as-performance-enhancer and gambling, and it is
        framed as clinical screening whereas the source is a social-service information-gathering
        conversation. Why this target: no single standard concept spans all five Swedish
        lifestyle-behavior domains; the substance-abuse screening procedure is the largest overlapping
        standard. Why related (not broader): the source is an information-gathering activity ABOUT
        behaviors (not a case of a behavior), and the target covers only a slice (3 of 5 domains); the
        activity-vs-procedure and partial-coverage gaps make the honest label rather than (the target
        does not subsume the source) or (the source is not a multi-part combination code in the partial
        sense, it is a combined-domain activity). 370854007 verified standard via self-Maps-to in
        athena/SNOMED/relationships.tdl.
        """
}
